    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "I couldn't apply it directly because it still had `queue.push({ method, payload });`. So I talked to Jonathan and he gave me this snippet:\r\n\r\n```js\r\n  type MethodNames = keyof InsightsMethodMap;\r\n  type Params<MethodName extends MethodNames> = [\r\n    method: MethodName,\r\n    ...args: InsightsMethodMap[MethodName]\r\n  ];\r\n  type ParamsMap = {\r\n    [MethodName in MethodNames]: Params<MethodName>;\r\n  };\r\n  globalObject.aa = <\r\n    MethodName extends MethodNames,\r\n    T extends ParamsMap[MethodName]\r\n  >(\r\n    ...params: T\r\n  ) => {\r\n    globalObject.aa!.queue = globalObject.aa!.queue || [];\r\n    globalObject.aa!.queue.push(params);\r\n  };\r\n```\r\n\r\nOnce we bind the method and arguments as one type, then the issue goes away. `queue.push()` no longer give us an error. However, now that we made a new type for the function to make it pass, we cannot assign it back to `globalObject.aa` due to type mismatch.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2021-10-28 at 10 38 32](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/499898/139219537-d411de7d-a24d-4167-b947-d00d54311884.png)\r\n\r\n",
    "commit_id": "b701ad6d5a850b1e5a9a60eb0d2eeec026aeb8c4",
    "created_at": "2021-10-28T08:40:05Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -17,11 +21,14 @@ export function createInsights() {\n }\n \n export function createInsightsUmdVersion() {\n-  const globalObject: any = {};\n-  globalObject.AlgoliaAnalyticsObject = 'aa';\n-  globalObject.aa = (...args) => {\n-    globalObject.aa.queue = globalObject.aa.queue || [];\n-    globalObject.aa.queue.push(args);\n+  const globalObject: { AlgoliaAnalyticsObject: string; aa?: InsightsClient } =\n+    {\n+      AlgoliaAnalyticsObject: 'aa',\n+    };\n+  globalObject.aa = (methodName, ...args) => {\n+    globalObject.aa!.queue = globalObject.aa!.queue || [];\n+    // @ts-ignore not sure why this is failing\n+    globalObject.aa!.queue.push([methodName, ...args]);",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch/pull/4932#discussion_r738168462",
